{"type":"message","id":"b537e1f1","parentId":"6f84bd03","timestamp":"2026-09-24T06:07:51.285Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# TASK: Fix every dependent of tau, then fork the major packages\n\nTwo objectives, in this order:\n\n  1. FIND AND FIX all dependents of tau. A dependent is anything that\n     references, invokes, imports, wraps, or points at tau — the binary,\n     the repo, the data directory, the engine packages, or the fork itself.\n     Broken dependents get repaired. Stale dependents get updated. Aliased\n     dependents get un-aliased.\n\n  2. FORK MAJOR. The packages tau depends on that are currently used\n     un-forked (hardlinked, symlinked, or read directly from vendor) get\n     their own fork under the canonical namespace. \"Major\" = a package\n     with its own source tree, its own build, and its own version. \"Minor\"\n     = a leaf script or asset; leave those.\n\nDo not start with edits. Discovery first. Then classify. Then fix.\n\n# PHASE 0 — Establish what tau is\n\nConfirm the identity of tau before finding dependents. Run and report:\n\n  which tau && readlink -f \"$(which tau)\"\n  file \"$(readlink -f \"$(which tau)\")\"\n  tau --version\n  ls -la ~/.tau/\n  ls -la ~/sovereign/projects/tau/ 2>/dev/null | head -20\n\nThree facts must be established and printed:\n  - the resolved path of the tau binary\n  - the tau version string\n  - the config/data directory that tau reads at startup\n\nCheck the environment:\n\n  env | grep -E '^PI_|^TAU_|^OMP_' | sort\n\nReport. These are the env dependencies. Every one of them is a place a\ndependent may reference.\n\n# PHASE 1 — Map every dependent\n\nSearch for references to tau across the home directory and the fork tree.\nThis is discovery, not modification.\n\n  # 1a. Files referencing the tau binary or path\n  rg -l --hidden --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/.git/**' \\\n     --glob '!**/.bun/**' --glob '!**/scratch/**' \\\n     'dist/tau\\b|/home/toxic/.local/bin/tau\\b|/home/toxic/.local/bin/tau\\b|\\btau\\b.*\\bacp\\b|PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR|PI_CONFIG_DIR' \\\n     ~/sovereign ~/.config ~/.local/bin ~/.tau 2>/dev/null \\\n     | sort -u > /tmp/deps-files.txt\n\n  wc -l /tmp/deps-files.txt\n\n  # 1b. Running processes that depend on tau\n  ps -ef | grep -E '\\btau\\b|cli\\.ts|dist/tau' | grep -v grep\n\n  # 1c. Daemons that launch tau\n  grep -rn 'tau\\|dist/tau\\|cli\\.ts' \\\n    ~/sovereign/pitchfork.toml ~/sovereign/mise.toml 2>/dev/null\n\n  # 1d. Launcher scripts and wrappers\n  find ~/sovereign/projects/tau/launcher \\\n       ~/.local/bin -maxdepth 2 \\\n       -name '*tau*' -o -name '*omp*' 2>/dev/null\n\n  # 1e. Skills that reference tau commands\n  rg -l --glob '**/SKILL.md' '\\btau\\b' ~/sovereign/skills 2>/dev/null\n\n  # 1f. Extensions that depend on tau\n  find ~/.tau/extensions ~/.tau/agent/extensions -name '*.ts' 2>/dev/null\n\n  # 1g. Package manifests that depend on tau\n  rg -l --hidden --glob '**/package.json' '\".*tau.*\"|dist/tau' \\\n     ~/sovereign 2>/dev/null | head -30\n\n  # 1h. Nix / Docker / systemd that reference tau\n  rg -l --hidden 'dist/tau|/home/toxic/.local/bin/tau' \\\n     ~/sovereign/projects/tau/engine/nix \\\n     ~/sovereign/docker 2>/dev/null\n\nReport the union of all discovered dependent paths, deduplicated, as a\ntable:\n\n  | # | path | type | references | status |\n\nDo not proceed until the table is printed.\n\n# PHASE 2 — Classify every dependent\n\nFor each dependent from Phase 1, classify as one of:\n\n  OK        — points at the canonical tau path and works\n  STALE     — points at a path that no longer exists (e.g., dist/tau)\n  ALIASED   — resolves via symlink or hardlink to another location\n  BROKEN    — references tau but fails at runtime\n  FOREIGN   — references tau but belongs to a different tool\n\nTo classify, for each dependent:\n\n  # If the dependent is a file:\n  rg -n 'dist/tau|/home/toxic/.local/bin/tau|/home/toxic/.local/bin/tau|cli\\.ts' <file>\n\n  # If the reference is a path, test it:\n  test -e <referenced-path> && echo EXISTS || echo MISSING\n\n  # If the path is a symlink:\n  readlink -f <path>\n\n  # If the file has link count > 1 (hardlink):\n  stat -c '%h %n' <file>\n\nProduce a classification table:\n\n  | # | path | status | reason | fix required |\n\nPrint it in full. This is the fix plan. Do not edit anything yet.\n\n# PHASE 3 — The fork integrity check\n\nBefore fixing dependents, verify the fork is actually a fork.\n\n  # 3a. engine vs vendor hardlink count\n  find ~/sovereign/engine/packages -type f -links +1 2>/dev/null | wc -l\n  find ~/sovereign/projects/tau/vendor/oh-my-pi/packages -type f -links +1 2>/dev/null | wc -l\n\nIf either count is nonzero, engine and vendor share inodes. Editing one\nsilently edits the other. This must be fixed before any dependent touches\neither tree.\n\n  # 3b. engine vs vendor content drift\n  diff -rq ~/sovereign/engine/packages \\\n           ~/sovereign/projects/tau/vendor/oh-my-pi/packages 2>/dev/null \\\n    | head -30\n\n  # 3c. symlinked packages\n  find ~/sovereign/engine/packages -maxdepth 1 -type l 2>/dev/null\n\n  # 3d. Which packages are actually under source control as forks\n  cd ~/sovereign && git ls-files engine/packages | cut -d/ -f3 | sort -u\n\nReport whether each major package is:\n  - a real fork (own files, own version, own git tracking)\n  - a hardlinked alias (link count > 1)\n  - a symlink to vendor\n  - a copy that is stale\n\n# PHASE 4 — Fix every dependent\n\nWork through the Phase 2 classification table in order. For each STALE,\nALIASED, or BROKEN dependent:\n\n  STALE fix — repoint the reference. If a file says `dist/tau`, change it\n  to `dist/tau`. If a manifest says `/home/toxic/.local/bin/tau`, change it to `/home/toxic/.local/bin/tau`.\n  Preserve the file's existing style (JSON, TOML, YAML, shell).\n\n  ALIASED fix — if the dependent resolves through a symlink or hardlink\n  to a path that is not canonical, replace the alias with a real copy or\n  a direct reference. Do not leave an alias in place.\n\n  BROKEN fix — repair the invocation. Read what the file expects, read\n  what the current tau actually provides, and update the call. If the\n  gap is not obvious, stop and report; do not guess.\n\n  FOREIGN — leave alone. Note in the report as out-of-scope.\n\nUse edit tools, not sed, for structured files (JSON, TOML, YAML).\nUse write for shell scripts and TS source.\n\nAfter each fix, re-run the classification test that identified the issue.\nConfirm the file now classifies as OK. If not, revert that one change\nwith the edit tool and mark it UNRESOLVED.\n\nPause after every 10 fixes. Print \"N done, M unresolved\". Do not continue\npast a BREAK decision without printing.\n\n# PHASE 5 — Fork major\n\nEnumerate the packages tau depends on. In ~/sovereign there are two trees:\n\n  vendor/oh-my-pi/packages/       — the upstream mirror\n  engine/packages/                — the fork tree\n\nFor each package under engine/packages/:\n\n  A. If it is a hardlink to vendor, or a symlink to vendor, or absent:\n       Replace with a real fork:\n         rm -rf ~/sovereign/engine/packages/<pkg>\n         cp -a --no-preserve=links \\\n           ~/sovereign/projects/tau/vendor/oh-my-pi/packages/<pkg> \\\n           ~/sovereign/engine/packages/<pkg>\n       Verify link count is 1:\n         find ~/sovereign/engine/packages/<pkg> -type f -links +1 | wc -l\n       The count must be 0. If not, the cp failed to break hardlinks;\n       use `rsync -a --no-links` or `tar -cf - | tar -xf -` to force\n       fresh inodes.\n\n  B. If it is a real copy already (link count 1) but has diverged from\n     vendor in ways you do not recognize, list the diff for user review.\n     Do not overwrite.\n\n  C. If it is a package the fork does not need (leaves, benchmarks,\n     test fixtures), skip it. Report as skipped.\n\nMajor packages that must be real forks (based on tau's runtime imports):\n\n  coding-agent, agent, ai, tui, utils, catalog, metaharness,\n  snapcompact, mnemopi, wire, omptype, natives, collab-web,\n  browser-relay, stats\n\nFor each, after forking:\n\n  # Verify it is a real fork\n  find ~/sovereign/engine/packages/<pkg> -type f -links +1 | wc -l   # 0\n  # Verify it has its own build metadata\n  cat ~/sovereign/engine/packages/<pkg>/package.json | head -20\n  # Verify vendor is untouched\n  find ~/sovereign/projects/tau/vendor/oh-my-pi/packages/<pkg> \\\n       -type f -links +1 | wc -l   # 0\n\nPrint for each major package: name, fork status, vendor untouched, own\nversion, own commit history if any.\n\n# PHASE 6 — Fix the engine-level workspace metadata\n\nThe engine needs a workspace file that declares its own packages as the\nfork's packages, not vendor's.\n\n  - If ~/sovereign/engine/package.json exists, verify its \"workspaces\"\n    array points at engine/packages/*, not vendor.\n  - If it does not exist, create a minimal one:\n\n    {\n      \"name\": \"sovereign-engine\",\n      \"private\": true,\n      \"workspaces\": [\"packages/*\"]\n    }\n\n  - Verify the resolution: from ~/sovereign/engine, running\n    `bun pm ls` should list the engine packages with their own versions,\n    not vendor's.\n\n  - If any engine package is a symlink back to vendor in the workspace\n    resolution, break it: replace with a real directory.\n\nReport the workspace resolution table.\n\n# PHASE 7 — Re-run the dependent scan\n\nRepeat Phase 1. Every dependent that classified as STALE, ALIASED, or\nBROKEN must now classify as OK, or be explicitly listed as UNRESOLVED.\n\nPrint the before/after classification counts:\n\n  Phase 2: OK=N STALE=N ALIASED=N BROKEN=N FOREIGN=N\n  Phase 7: OK=N STALE=N ALIASED=N BROKEN=N FOREIGN=N UNRESOLVED=N\n\nUNRESOLVED count must be 0 for the task to be complete, or each one is\njustified with a one-line reason.\n\n# PHASE 8 — Global verification\n\nRun all of these. Paste the output of each.\n\n  # 8a. Engine is a real fork\n  find ~/sovereign/engine/packages -type f -links +1 | wc -l     # 0\n  find ~/sovereign/projects/tau/vendor/oh-my-pi/packages \\\n       -type f -links +1 | wc -l                                 # 0\n\n  # 8b. No engine symlinks remain\n  find ~/sovereign/engine/packages -maxdepth 1 -type l | wc -l    # 0\n\n  # 8c. tau runs\n  tau --version\n\n  # 8d. Audit scripts pass\n  bash ~/.local/bin/tau-audit.sh 2>&1 | tail -1\n  bun run ~/sovereign/skills/tau-tmux/helper/audit.ts 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n  # 8e. Live daemons reference the canonical path\n  ps -ef | grep -E '\\btau\\b|dist/tau' | grep -v grep\n\n  # 8f. Every manifest that references tau points at dist/tau, not dist/tau\n  rg -n 'dist/tau' ~/sovereign ~/.config ~/.local/bin 2>/dev/null \\\n    --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/.git/**' | wc -l   # 0\n\n  # 8g. Every skill under ~/sovereign/skills references the correct\n  #     binary name\n  rg -n '\\bomp\\b' ~/sovereign/skills --glob '**/SKILL.md' 2>/dev/null | wc -l\n\nIf 8a or 8b is nonzero, the fork is not a fork. Do not declare done.\nIf 8f is nonzero, there are still stale references to the old name.\nIf any other check fails, report the failure with the exact command and\noutput.\n\n# RULES\n\n- Discovery before edits. Do not touch a file until Phase 1 has produced\n  the full dependent table.\n- Classify before fixing. Phase 2's table is the plan. Phase 4 executes\n  the plan. No opportunistic edits.\n- Fork integrity (Phase 3) comes before dependent fixes. If engine and\n  vendor share inodes, fixing dependents does nothing — the next edit\n  to engine silently edits vendor.\n- Every fix is verified by re-running the classification test. If a fix\n  does not reclassify as OK, revert it and mark UNRESOLVED.\n- Do not delete any file. Do not move any file into place from outside\n  the tree without first copying and verifying. `cp -a --no-preserve=links`\n  is the only sanctioned way to materialize a fork.\n- Do not commit to git until the user says so. `git add` and\n  `git diff --stat` are fine.\n- If a subagent is used, it handles exactly one phase. Do not parallelize\n  Phase 4 across files. Do not parallelize Phase 5 across packages.\n- Print before/after counts for every phase. A phase that produces no\n  output is a phase that did not run."}],"attribution":"user","timestamp":1790230071246}}
